	)
	(text "PWM Channel Fiber Transmitters\n\n3-Phases of HRTIM-configurable PWM outputs are \navailable. Each phase's fiber optic transmitter\nset are driven an IX4340NTR gate driver with \nan enable tied to PWM_Enable. (see section for\nexplaination of logic)\n\nAs long as PWM_Enable is not pulled to ground\nan input V_INx > V_thresh will allow the Versatile\nLink TX fiber transmitters to be driven. This \nhappens when both Phase_S and Phase_SN are being \noutput, as computed by the inverter and AND logic\ngates.\n\n(PWM Alt Enable available to repurpose PWM outputs\nin other applications)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.614 263.906 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d06d9cdc-5e97-4bf2-bc51-96372469c559")
	)
	(text "AnalogIn_06"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 638.048 493.014 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d11159cd-519c-47b1-805e-5dbf5b620a9c")
	)
	(text "Gate Driver Status Receivers\n\nThe Gate Driver Status fiber\nsignals are received by 12 Versatile\nLink RX fiber receivers.\n\nLogic of this device is configured to\nallow selection between Normally\nHIGH GDS and Normally LOW GDS to allow\ncontrol of both the old and new HVPS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 516.636 252.984 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d9b7ae65-ec39-4dd3-8bee-55bd2ec09316")
	)
	(text "USART2_RX"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 209.55 110.744 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "db584ccd-c531-49bc-841b-e1ef68f624eb")
	)
	(text "ADC5_IN1"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 200.152 92.964 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "df121714-d28c-4334-a6eb-a3a0faaea76d")
	)
	(text "&"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 411.48 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "df6574fd-b2ed-4540-b8fb-75dcb0ea7481")
	)
	(text "GPOut Fiber Transmitters\n\nThere are 12 general purpose Versatile Link\nTX transmitters. Transmitters are organized in\npairs of 2, although can be operated indepen-\ndently of each partner. \n\nEach pair is driven by\na 2-Ch IX4340NTR to level shift +3.3V STM32\nGPO logic level to +5V needed to drive the \nVersatile Link transmitters. [Strictly speaking\nthis is not necessary with proper choice of \nseries resistor].\n\nEach pair of GPO fiber outputs can be enabled\nor disabled by software control ouf the\nGPOut_Enable_Pin on the STM32G4 MCU. \n\nAdditionally, one pair of transmitters has been\nselected for alternate use as USART1_TX and \nUSART3_TX allowing for easy serial communication\nover two possible fiber optic lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 714.502 310.388 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e06e396c-9166-4299-8ab0-12b4cf007a17")
	)
